      "text": "2.9. Fluoride analysis and kinetic calculations Fluoride ions (F \u207b ) released during photocatalytic treatment were quantified by ion chromatography (IC; Dionex ICS-2100) using a Met - rohm IonPac AS14 column with an eluent of 4.5 mM Na \u2082 CO \u2083 / 1.4 mM NaHCO \u2083 at 1.0 mL min \u207b \u00b9. Samples were filtered (0.22 \u00b5 m), diluted, and analyzed in triplicate. Calibration standards (0.05 \u2013 10 mg L \u207b \u00b9 F \u207b ) were used to determine fluoride concentrations; reported values are mean \u00b1 SD (n = 3). Apparent rate constants (k \u1d43\u1d56\u1d56 ) for PFAS disappearance were esti - mated using a pseudo-first-order approximation from the 120 min data point for comparative purposes via: K app = \u0000 1 t ln ( C 0 C t ) (2) Where C 0 and C t are the PFAS concentrations at time 0 and t = 120 min, respectively. K app values reported here provide a simple metric to quantify matrix-induced slowing of apparent reaction rates. Total fluorine (TF) by combustion ion chromatography (CIC) is recommended for achieving a full fluorine mass balance. Where possible, TF should be measured on aliquots of (i) initial PFAS solution,"
